cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NIC-Heimdall in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "NIC-Heimdall: an open multi-phenomenon geophysical station (concept)"
version: "0.2"
date-released: 2026-10-04
authors:
  - name: "NIC — Native Intellect Community"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Project-NIC/NIC-Heimdall"
license:
  - CERN-OHL-S-2.0
  - MIT
abstract: >-
  A design-stage open concept for a self-contained measuring station that records
  seismic motion, the geomagnetic field, lightning and sferics, the ionosphere
  (GNSS TEC, HF and longwave), ionising radiation, sea-floor pressure and the
  weather on one clocked bus, with a self-describing archive (HMC) and its
  lossless codec (HCC), and exporters to the formats of the world's networks
  (miniSEED, IAGA-2002, RINEX, BUFR). Nothing has been built yet; the documents
  are the design.
keywords:
  - citizen science
  - open hardware
  - geophysics
  - seismology
  - geomagnetism
  - lightning detection
  - ionosphere
  - space weather
  - radiation monitoring
  - meteorology
  - sensor network
  - data logger
